# Raw ingested data (regenerated via ingest scripts)
data/

# Static Bible/commentary files (generated by ingest scripts, too large for git)
# Deploy with `npx vercel` from web/ which reads local files directly
# NOTE: each corpus path is listed BOTH with and without a trailing slash. The slash form
# matches only a DIRECTORY, so a dev-convenience SYMLINK of the same name slipped past `git add -A`
# and shipped absolute local paths to main (bb8ef05). The slashless form catches that.
web/public/bible/
web/public/bible
web/public/commentaries/
web/public/commentaries
# Same pattern: generated interlinear + lexicon static data
web/public/lexicon/
web/public/lexicon
web/public/original/
web/public/original
# Generated by scripts/build-corpus-manifest.mjs so GET /api/health can name the corpus it
# serves. The COMMITTED record is docs/evidence/corpus-manifest-<sha>-<ts>.json; this copy
# only ships inside the artifact, and committing it would let the two disagree.
web/public/corpus-manifest.json

# Generated coverage report + Neon CLI project artifact
coverage/
.neon

# Throwaway SEC-2/auth spike workspace (own node_modules + local-only secrets)
spike/
.vercel

# Entries lifted OUT of web/public/commentaries by src/ingest/quarantine-served-corpus.ts so the
# static artifact stops DELIVERING what the reader already refuses to RENDER (deep audit C2).
# Deliberately outside web/, which is the Vercel upload root — that is the whole point. Same
# reason as the corpus itself: too large for git, and it holds the must-not-serve content.
corpus-quarantine/

# transient re-source verification cache
.newadvent-cache/
web/public/concordance/
web/public/concordance

.env.prod
.cutover-checkpoint.json
.env*

# Agent scratch scripts. A dotfile .mjs at the repo root is a throwaway probe, never a deliverable.
# Added 2026-08-19 after an unscoped `git add -A` committed `.wc.mjs` (a watcher) in ec6b544, whose
# later deletion then BLOCKED a deploy — deploy.sh gates on a clean tree because `vercel --prod`
# uploads the working tree, so anything uncommitted would ship to production un-reviewed.
/.*.mjs
